      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #11b, 2026-08-06): a partial
      ⍝ shape product legitimately overflows int64 when a later axis is
      ⍝ 0 (the overflowing partial product is intentionally discarded,
      ⍝ per design comments in Shape.hh/Shape.cc) -- but doing that via
      ⍝ plain "volume *= len" made the overflow itself UB rather than
      ⍝ just an intentionally-discarded value. Shape::add_shape_item()
      ⍝ and Shape::fits_into() now multiply via uint64_t (well-defined
      ⍝ wraparound) instead.
